window.EN={"1":"August, where is this...?","2":"We are already inside the temple of Loptr. Lord Leif, please be on your guard!","3":"I see... It's dark and I can't see anything... I wonder where Eyvel is.","4":"In any case, we have no choice but to go forward.","5":"Most likely one passes from the central magic circle through to the altar where Veld is.","6":"Prince, impatience is forbidden. Please be calm and advance cautiously.","7":"......","8":"Eyvel, hold on! Eyvel!","9":"......","10":"Eyvel, it's me, Leif! Don't you know me!","11":"...Lord... Leif... Leif...","12":"Ah! Lord Leif! Why are you here? Quickly, escape...","13":"Eyvel, no, it's not like that, Eyvel...","14":"Not like that? But this arena is... Huh? This place...","15":"Eyvel, thank goodness, you're back to yourself...","16":"Lord Leif, what on earth happened to me...","17":"I'm sorry. There's no time to talk right now.","18":"We are fighting now to liberate Munster... no, Thracia, from the Empire.","19":"Eyvel, I want you to lend me your strength!","20":"Of course I will, but... when the battle is over, will you tell me?","21":"Of course. Eyvel, there's so much I want to tell you...","22":"......","23":"Mother! Hold on! Mother!","24":"......","25":"Mother! Don't you know me?","26":"......","27":"Mother, I'm sorry... I... I...","28":"...Why are you crying... Mareeta...","29":"Huh... Mother?","30":"Thank goodness, you've come back to your senses. Come, quickly, away from here... Huh, this place...","31":"Mother! Thank goodness...","32":"Mareeta, where on earth is this... Why am I here?","33":"Mother, you were... turned to stone by Raydrik...","34":"To stone? ...Come to think of it, where is Raydrik?","35":"We defeated Raydrik. But the Loptr people are still... Mother, please, lend us your strength!","36":"Of course, Mareeta... I'm sorry, it seems I made you worry a great deal. I still have a long way to go myself...","37":"Mother...","38":"Eyvel... I've missed you...","39":"This past year, I fought the Empire dreaming of the day I could be reunited with you.","40":"And at last it has come true. Nothing could make me happier.","41":"Lord Leif... So a whole year has passed since then...","42":"Lord Leif, I truly hardly recognize you... You have become a fine sovereign.","43":"That, too, is all thanks to you, Eyvel. The three years in Fiana village were truly happy.","44":"Playing among the village youths, getting into fights...","45":"You scolded me many times, but I was glad even to be scolded.","46":"Finn was the father, you were the mother, Nanna and Mareeta were my sisters,","47":"and in the village I had friends like Osian and Halvan. I wished those days could go on forever.","48":"You were like a mother to me. It was a mother's warmth I had long forgotten.","49":"That day... with the gravely wounded Finn laid across a horse's back, the prince and Lady Nanna came to the village.","50":"Lady Nanna clung to me, her eyes brimming with tears, begging me to please save her father.","51":"But you, Lord Leif, glared at me, said \"If you help us I'll give you this,\" and only held out the sword at your waist...","52":"It was a keepsake of your mother, I was told. Still just a boy, yet you must have been through so much, I thought.","53":"Lord Leif, I have no memory of my younger days.","54":"A dozen or so years ago, I was found collapsed on the coast of Ith and saved by the villagers.","55":"Who am I... Did I have a husband... children... I don't even remember that.","56":"But when I saw the two of you, I realized something similar had happened in my own past.","57":"From that day, I thought of you as my own children, and resolved to raise you strictly.","58":"But I never dreamed you were the prince of Leonster...","59":"Eyvel... I was envious of Mareeta.","60":"If only I had my mother too, I could be spoiled the way Mareeta is... Thinking that, I cried many times.","61":"But you loved us without any distinction. I am truly grateful.","62":"Lady Nanna... You are a princess of the illustrious land of Nordion.","63":"The gallant blood of the paladin Hezul flows in your body too.","64":"Please have courage, and live alongside Lord Leif.","65":"Your mother is surely alive. Even I was able to be reunited like this.","66":"Don't give up. You will surely see her...","67":"Eyvel, you're a fine one. Even I, a man, am no match for you.","68":"Dagdar, I am grateful to you.","69":"That Fiana village was protected, and that I have lived to this day, is all thanks to you.","70":"Thank you, Dagdar...","71":"D-don't be silly... I-I only...","72":"Pops, what are you turning red for! Geez, you're so pathetic. Get a grip!!","73":"Lady Eyvel, to us young people of the village too, you were like a mother.","74":"My sister and I especially, having no parents, were as good as raised by you.","75":"That is why I... have fought to this day to get you back, Lady Eyvel.","76":"Halvan... I made you worry too.","77":"When this battle is over, let's go back to Fiana together. I'm sure Patricia is worried as well.","78":"A mother, huh... yeah. My ma's dead too, but my old man's still alive and kicking,","79":"and maybe even a guy like that is better than not having one...","80":"That's right, Osian. Compared to Halvan, you are still fortunate.","81":"When you get back to Fiana, take good care of your father.","82":"Mareeta? What's wrong? All alone over there...","83":"Mother...","84":"My, my, just like a child. Crying your eyes out like that spoils a pretty face.","85":"There, wipe your tears...","86":"Mother!... I... I...","87":"It's all right now. It's all right, Mareeta...","88":"You are...?","89":"I meant to leave just like this, but I wanted to say one thing after all.","90":"For raising... my daughter this far... I thank you.","91":"Oh!?... You are Mareeta's...","92":"That's right... Her mother died soon after bearing this child, and afterward we traveled together.","93":"But in the brief moment I took my eyes off her, she was stolen by slave traders...","94":"In the slave market in the town of Connacht, a still innocent little girl was chained up and being sold.","95":"Seeing that, in my rage I killed the slave traders and their guards, every one...","96":"When I undid the girl's chains and asked her name, she told me it was Mareeta.","97":"She said she had been with her father until a little while before, so I searched the area at once, but I couldn't find you.","98":"No... I was the one at fault... Traveling with a small child was impossible from the start.","99":"My daughter was fortunate to be taken in by you.","100":"You may think it presumptuous of me, but would you go on looking after my daughter from here on...?","101":"Yes, of course.","102":"Mareeta is already my daughter... Even if you wished it, I have no intention of letting her go.","103":"I see... When this job is done I'll set out on the road again. We will likely never meet again.","104":"Swordsman Galzus, I have just one request of you.","105":"What is it? If it is something I can do, I will do anything...","106":"Would you stop by Fiana village just once a year? I ask for nothing more...","107":"...... All right... I will...","108":"Eyvel... I'm sorry for all the trouble. I, too, must thank you.","109":"It is you who have worked hard, Finn.","110":"There is surely no knight like you even if one searched this whole continent. I truly think you are admirable.","111":"Eyvel...","112":"I had thought not to speak of this, but hearing your talk with Lord Leif just now, I can no longer keep silent.","113":"I know someone who closely resembles you...","114":"Me...? This is the first I've heard of it. Finn, is that true...?","115":"Yes... When I was fighting alongside Lord Quan, there was a woman warrior in Sigurd's army.","116":"With her long blonde hair streaming as she stood on the battlefield, she was so beautiful one might have taken her for a goddess.","117":"She was a princess of House Jungby, heir to the holy bow Yewfelle... Her name... was Brigid...","118":"Brigid...? Finn, do you mean to say that person is me?","119":"Yes... Probably...","120":"Heehee... You are unexpectedly a romantic, Finn.","121":"If I were one who inherited the blood of the crusaders, there ought to be a Brand somewhere on my body. But there is no such thing anywhere.","122":"Finn, you are mistaken. I am just a traveling mercenary. Eyvel of Fiana village..."};
